<title>HONG KONG: Pearl Oriental 1996 net rises 74.1 pct.</title>
<headline>Pearl Oriental 1996 net rises 74.1 pct.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-03-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended December 31</p>
<p>(in million HK$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (H.K. cents)	   15.9	  vs 11.0 (adjusted)</p>
<p>    Dividend (H.K. cents)    6.0	   vs 4.3 (adjusted)</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	  245.42 gain vs 227.91 gain</p>
<p>    Net			    714.56	vs 410.34</p>
<p>    Turnover		     1,551.06    vs 1,058.97</p>
<p>    Company name		 Pearl Oriental Holdings Ltd</p>
<p>    Books close		  April 18-23</p>
<p>    Dividend payable	   April 30</p>
<p>NOTE - Pearl Oriental engages in commercial property trading and development, project management, hotel management and consultancy services.</p>
<p>The company proposed a bonus issue on the basis of one-for-one share held.</p>
<p>Net is after an exceptional gain on forfeiters of deposit from pre-sale of properties.</p>
<p>Comparative share earnings and final dividend have been adjusted to take account of the two-for-one bonus issue during the year 1996.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6368</p>
</text>
